# Vidya (egui theme)

Browse paints UI through **Vidya**. Prefer existing Vidya widgets/layout helpers over raw egui.

## Repos

| Source | URL |
|--------|-----|
| GitHub (mirror, Cloud Agent clone) | https://github.com/codegod100/vidya |
| Tangled (canonical) | https://tangled.org/nandi.uk/vidya |
| Radicle | [`rad:z2UqGTRH21s3pHnJgSuMwRaPPNNcW`](https://nandi.radicle.garden/rad:z2UqGTRH21s3pHnJgSuMwRaPPNNcW) |

## Local paths

- Cloud Agent install clones to **`$HOME/.local/share/vidya`** (see [`.cursor/environment.json`](../environment.json)).
- When a sibling checkout exists, Cargo expects **`../vidya`** (`path` dep in `Cargo.toml`).
- Nix builds pull Vidya from the flake input (no sibling required).

When changing theme tokens, widgets, or layout DSL behavior, read the Vidya tree first and reuse its API (`Theme`, `primary_button`, `card`, `lead_trail`, `page_body` / grid DSL, etc.) instead of inventing parallel chrome.
